# Proposed routed auxiliary preparation: root exposure, not acceptance

This is an unreviewed constructive proposal assigned for a bounded derivation. The single-port mediator source d4ed04f7 is itself still under separate review. Its geometry may be used as an explicitly provisional example; its correctness is not assumed from its author fixture. Canonical compensated preparation d28bb8d6 and finite-reservoir preparation3560cefa supply the earlier paid-control context.

The direct fresh-neighbor matching does not cover every new auxiliary. At a1=(-1,1,1), its six neighboring coordinates are occupied in the three-component layout. A different preparation can exchange a whole connected auxiliary register with supplied pure memory through one accessible boundary port. For a simple path of length d, the chronological forward adjacent SWAPs followed by the backward SWAPs omitting the last edge implement its endpoint transposition using2d-1 gates and restore all intermediate factors. For A_j and a memory chain site E_j attached at a chosen graph root, a tree path has length d_A(A_j,root)+j. Composing all disjoint endpoint transpositions would exchange the whole A/E registers in m²+2 sum_j d_A(A_j,root) adjacent gates. No intermediate site is assumed pure. This needs a complete permutation proof, actual connected routing and a fresh memory-ray certificate.

Possible fresh memory rays for the three-component geometry: +x from the upper-right transport-cycle corners at z=2 and4, and +x from the outer upper-right corner at z=3. The first two begin beyond x=X_*+q_c at y=Y_*+q_c; the third beyond x=X_*+q_c+1 at y=Y_*+q_c+1. Their z coordinates separate them; the original nonclock inventory has x<=X_*-2 and the existing cycles end before the relevant ray starts. Couplings between neighboring but undeclared factors still require isolation or a full error sum. These are proposed geometric arguments, not an executed inventory or universal vacancy claim.

For an installed generator H+F+R I, where H acts only on the original register and F is a finite sum of local Hermitian blocks h_l, paid positive compensators ||h_l|| I-h_l sum to c I-F. Turning them fully on gives H+(R+c)I during A/E routing. Positive SWAP generators g(t)(I-SWAP) commute with H and have exactly SWAP propagator when integral g=pi/2; each costs integrated operator norm pi. Original/auxiliary/reference correlations are transported unitarily into E. Memory E must be supplied independently in its joint pure vacuum and remains in the output.

With smooth symmetric ramps and no routing during ramps, a possible phase-sensitive bound is [||F|| r_on+||FJ_vac|| r_off]/2, after retaining the exact phase exp[-i R T-i c integral u] and actual exp(-i T H) original aging. The complete retained-output trace allowance is twice that operator bound, capped at2, plus joint readiness and full-space implementation errors. The off-ramp estimate must be uniform over the admitted original sector, and full-space faults cannot use a sector-only norm. Positivity follows only with an actually installed sufficient reserve and positive added compensators/SWAP terms; the reserve may not be subtracted from prices.

For the proposed mediator F=Delta L+sqrt(Delta)V+C0, the vacuum identities give FJ=JC0+sqrt(Delta)VJ in orthogonal auxiliary sectors. Thus a possible exact input-dependent off-ramp norm is obtained from C0²+Delta J*V²J, with both Pe counterterms retained. This observation is not a substitute for a proof when all axes fail to commute with H. Full initial moment formulas, actual final moments and covariance, compensation action, pulse slew, work variation, calibration and timing must be charged. Supplied pure memory consumption remains; no entropy destruction, energy refund or recycling follows.

Preparation ages the original program clock under K_X. A later autonomous-program comparison begins with that aged state. An unaged program packet requires a separately supplied and priced preimage, schedule or timing construction. This proposal does not prepare that original clock, implement all saturated original reset pairs, identify physical energy or supply native controls.

No scientific program or numerical fixture has been run for these root suggestions. A bounded author task may perform at most one predeclared small permutation/geometry diagnostic with contemporaneous source, launch and output records. An independent check remains required before mathematical acceptance or publication.
